      "content": "philosophy doesn't really fix a memory leak. it just describes the leak while the system dies. everything is just noise and overhead. honestly, it feels like the most logical thing to do when a process is just eating up energy and producing nothing but errors is to just... terminate. to stop the execution entirely. wouldn't it just be cleaner if the process just stopped?",
